    "42C key_click_event5EEA90 loads5EEB1F and calls5EEB2B, callerpop8, keeps EAX and adds virtual result.434 key_up_event5EEDC0 loads5EEE22/calls5EEE2C/callerpop4 and retains EAX; on_key5F5D10 loads5F5E91/calls5F5E9C/callerpop4 and ignores EAX. Preserve signed argument bit patterns, guards, focused-child early consumption, callback publication and sound order. Existing typed400/408/430/438 remain unchanged.",
    "Win ctor5EB3D0 clears fields404..434 (4045EB5C3,40C5EB5CF,4345EB60B); close5EB640 clears them (4345EBC04). Current source has no nonzero installer; that remains an original dependency, not proof of whole-executable absence. Source member names may stay neutral; do not invent original callback declarations or setters.",
    "window_proc5F0650 loads existing Sound* AutoSound val6 at5F0940, pushes5F0943, calls5F86A0 at5F0946. Helper null-tests stack argument, calls existing Sound slots23/7 and ret4, ignores play result. Replace false int-to-Win-to-Sound boundary with Sound*, retain original helper identity/name; coordinator publishes compiler-proven current symbol using native writer. No outside source owner edit indicated.",
    "Fixtures must use real callable pointers and retain all branch/order/mutant assertions. Baseline focused scan59pass3fail1skip: two left_down fixture Sound members still intptr and one obsolete fixed-body-equality test fail. Authorize typed Sound fixture repair and retiring only that permanent pre-annotation body-text freeze (not identity/spans/claims/provenance tests); subsequent faithful structural recovery cannot be forbidden by a fixed old body. Preserve original task baseline and every historical matching obligation. No bug fixes, manual ORIGINAL edits, new claims or flags."
